I haven't tested it and the checks are case sensitive, but wouldn't this work?
```
        if ( query.startsWith( "SELECT new " )) {
        	throw new PanacheQueryException("Unable to use .project with 'select new' query");
        }

        if ( query.startsWith( "SELECT " ) || query.startsWith("select ")) {
        	int endSelect= query.indexOf( " from " );
        	String from = query.substring( endSelect );
        	StringBuilder newQuery = new StringBuilder("SELECT new " )
        			.append(type.getName())
        			.append(" (")
        			.append( query.substring( "SELECT ".length(), endSelect ) )
        			.append( ")" )
        			.append( from );

        	return new CommonPanacheQueryImpl<>(this, newQuery.toString(), "select count(*) " + from);
        }
```

It's not perfect, but I think it would work for most common scenarios
